<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Privacy manifest for the notification service extension.

  An app extension is a separate bundle with its own executable, and Apple
  reads a manifest per bundle. The app's own PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy at
  ios/App/App/ does not cover this target, so without this file the extension
  is simply undeclared in the aggregated privacy report.

  Everything below is empty on purpose, and each entry is a claim about code
  that can be checked against NotificationService.swift:

  - NSPrivacyTracking = false. The extension talks to mytrivia.io (the push
    icon) and to whatever https URL the payload names as the sender avatar.
    Neither is an ad network and nothing is joined with data from other
    companies. The app target keeps NSPrivacyTracking = true because AdMob
    runs there; this bundle contains no ad SDK at all.

  - NSPrivacyTrackingDomains empty. Adding a domain here makes iOS block it
    until ATT is authorised — which would break icon downloads for every
    player who declined tracking, for no reason.

  - NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes empty. Nothing is collected: the extension
    reads the push it was handed, downloads two images, and hands the
    notification back. The INInteraction donation stays on device.

  - NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes empty. It links no third-party frameworks
    (its Frameworks build phase is empty) and touches no required-reason
    API. FileManager.temporaryDirectory / moveItem / removeItem are not on
    the list; the file-timestamp APIs are, and none is called here.

  If this extension ever gains an SDK or starts reading file timestamps,
  this file has to grow with it or the upload is rejected.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>

	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>

	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>

	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
